# BAWAAL Arena Challenge Architecture (LOCKED baseline)

High-performance stealth-black sports network centered on **asynchronous 1v1 video battles**.
Further work builds on this contract — do not regress the single video Arena feed, inline community shelf, slim FACEOFF hub, BATTLES open callouts, 1-tap challenge camera, or post-record teardown.

## Core mechanics

- Side-by-side battle cards: **YOU / opener on the left** vs **challenger on the right** (`ArenaFeed.js` `BattleCard`).
- Open challenges: left = host benchmark (`@YOU`), right = empty RESPOND slot until athletes reply.
- Primary surface: `ArenaFeed.js` (Arena tab). Camera: `UniversalCamera.tsx`.

## Single video Arena feed (`ArenaFeed.js`)

- Main Arena is a **clutter-free cinematic video feed** — no dual-segment toggle, no horizontal category pill scroller on the feed chrome, **no floating toast/notification banners** over video.
- Header: **ARENA** + top-right **FACEOFF** action.
- **Inline shelf:** every **4–5** media items, inject a horizontal **🔥 LIVE COMMUNITY CHALLENGES** row (`CommunityChallengesShelf`) with OPEN CHALLENGES + TIPS & BREAKDOWNS cards (RESPOND / TEACH). Tap → `openBattlesCallout(id)` deep-links into BATTLES.

## FACEOFF hub (scores + sports only)

- Tap **FACEOFF** opens a dedicated hub containing:
  1. Live sports scores ticker (`ScoresSportsPanel` — B&W monochromatic).
  2. Sports category grid (locked taxonomy).
- Do **not** reintroduce Open Callouts lists or floating Arena toasts.

## BATTLES tab — Open Callouts (source of truth)

- `BattlesScreen.js` hosts **Active Battles** and **Open Callouts**.
- Open Callouts use two categories (`src/utils/faceoffCallout.js`):
  - **OPEN CHALLENGES** — performance, benchmark, or 1v1 action callouts.
  - **TIPS & BREAKDOWNS** — technique, advice, or form-check requests.
- UI panel: `src/components/OpenCalloutsPanel.js`.
- Arena shelf deep-link focuses the matching callout via `focusChallengeId`.

